2. HMRC figures: Crown copyright, Open Government Licence v3.0
--------------------------------------------------------------

The trade values, masses and commodity descriptions in
data/uk-china-import-pulse.csv and data/uk-china-export-pulse.csv, and the figures we derived from them (totals,
percentage changes, GBP per kg), come from HM Revenue & Customs Overseas Trade
Statistics (https://www.uktradeinfo.com/). They are Crown copyright and are
used and may be reused under the Open Government Licence v3.0:
https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/

Anyone reusing them must keep this attribution:

    Contains HMRC data © Crown copyright 2026, licensed under the Open
    Government Licence v3.0.

As the OGL requires, reuse must not suggest that HMRC or the Crown endorses
Cambridge China Bridge, you, or your use of the information. The OGL does not
grant rights in HMRC's logos or other marks.

3. Eurostat figures: re-use with acknowledgement of the source
-------------------------------------------------------------

The trade values, masses and product labels in data/china-eu-trade-pulse.csv
come from Eurostat's Comext database (dataset DS-045409, imports from China by
EU member state, https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/comext/newxtweb/). Eurostat's
copyright notice (https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/help/copyright-notice) states:
"Reuse of statistical data, metadata, publications, and other dissemination
tools published on this website for commercial or non-commercial purposes is
authorised provided the source is acknowledged." The European Commission's
reuse policy is implemented by the Commission Decision of 12 December 2011.

Acknowledgement: "Source: Eurostat."

Modifications, stated as the notice requires: Cambridge China Bridge summed
Eurostat's monthly figures into calendar quarters, calculated year-on-year
changes, rankings and value per kg, selected the rows shown, and changed
chapter labels from upper case to sentence case. Eurostat is not responsible
for these figures or for any use made of them.

4. Official Chinese holiday dates: public facts
-----------------------------------------------

The holiday periods and make-up working days with status "official" or
"provisional_statutory" are facts published by the State Council of the
People's Republic of China (notice 国办发明电〔2025〕7号 and the national
holiday regulations 全国年节及纪念日放假办法). We claim no rights in those
dates or in the government documents; we link to them as sources. Chinese
copyright law (Article 5 of the Copyright Law of the PRC) excludes official
documents of state organs from copyright protection.

No warranty
-----------

The data are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. HMRC revises
and Eurostat revise recent figures, and Chinese holiday arrangements are confirmed only by each
year's notice. Check the official sources before relying on a figure or a
date for a contract, a quotation or a shipment. Piggy Pineapple Ltd is not
liable for any loss arising from use of the data, to the extent the law
allows.
